00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:51,800
Well, they were both among the great mathematicians of the

220
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:52,800
20th century.

221
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:59,800
So, I think we, our knowledge of fat-tailed distribution

222
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:02,800
comes down to us through word of mouth.

223
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,800
From Lévy, who was Mandelbrot's teacher, to

224
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:07,800
Mandelbrot, to me, and then to you, I think.

225
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:11,800
So, we don't require any printed word to know this.

226
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:15,800
That's the way the history of thought goes.

227
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:18,800
So, there's an old joke about the normal distribution.

228
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:22,800
It said that, the joke goes as follows.

