Hank Greenberg, is going to talk about his company, AIG,

1278
01:14:33,800 --> 01:14:35,800
which failed because of errors.

1279
01:14:35,800 --> 01:14:36,800
It didn't fail.

1280
01:14:36,800 --> 01:14:37,800
It got bailed out by the government.

1281
01:14:37,800 --> 01:14:40,800
It got bailed out because of errors made in credit default

1282
01:14:40,800 --> 01:14:41,800
swaps.

1283
01:14:41,800 --> 01:14:45,800
I don't think that these errors were his fault, because this

1284
01:14:45,800 --> 01:14:47,800
happened after he left the company.

1285
01:14:47,800 --> 01:14:50,800
But I just want to mention this, because it's all part of a big

1286
01:14:50,800 --> 01:14:51,800
picture.

1287
01:14:51,800 --> 01:14:53,800
We had a financial invention, the swap.

1288
01:14:53,800 --> 01:14:56,800
Then we had the credit default swap.

1289
01:14:56,800 --> 01:14:58,800
And these are important inventions.

1290
01:14:58,800 --> 01:15:02,800
They caused a leap forward in our ability to do risk

1291
01:15:02,800 --> 01:15:05,800
management, but they created attendant risks.

1292
01:15:05,800 --> 01:15:07,800
They were new, and they weren't understood by the government.

1293
01:15:07,800 --> 01:15:09,800
They weren't understood well enough.

1294
01:15:09,800 --> 01:15:12,800
And so, a big part of what happened in this crisis was a

1295
01:15:12,800 --> 01:15:15,800
failure of the credit default swap market.

1296
01:15:15,800 --> 01:15:18,800
But that's not, to me, an indictment of financial

1297
01:15:18,800 --> 01:15:19,800
innovation.

1298
01:15:19,800 --> 01:15:23,800
I think the credit default swap was an important innovation,

1299
01:15:23,800 --> 01:15:27,800
and we will see more like it, and it will help make for a

1300
01:15:27,800 --> 01:15:28,800
better world.
